<title>THAILAND: Thai Jan-April petroleum demand up 7.9 percent.</title>
<headline>Thai Jan-April petroleum demand up 7.9 percent.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's petroleum demand during the first four months of this year grew by 7.9 percent over last year to 949,350 barrels per day (bpd), the Petroleum Authority of Thailand (PTT) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The demand for natural gas surged 34.5 percent during the same period to reach 196,520 bpd, most of which was used for power generation, PTT said in a statement.</p>
<p>Consumption of refined oil product averaged 749,830 bpd, or a drop of 2.0 percent over the same period last year.</p>
<p>PTT detailed petroleum use and procurement during the first four months as follows (in bpd):</p>
<p> Total consumption		Jan-April 1997  Change from 1996</p>
<p> Gas oil				     325,970	up  7.7 pct</p>
<p> Fuel oil				    155,870	dn 13.1 pct</p>
<p> Gasoline				    127,590	up  6.9 pct</p>
<p> Aviation fuel				63,510	up  5.8 pct</p>
<p> Liquid petroleum gas		     56,670	up  9.0 pct</p>
<p> Kerosene					1,570	dn 14.2 pct</p>
<p> Natural gas				 196,520	up 34.5 pct</p>
<p> Bitumen					12,520	up 30.8 pct</p>
<p> Lubricants				    6,310	up 13.3 pct</p>
<p> TOTAL					 949,350	up  7.9 pct</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
